# Requirements

### H1: Channel c0 drives the body forward

WHEN c0 is held at 0.5 for the first 1.0 s and c1 to c4 are 0, THE system SHALL end with x between 0.1 and 1.0 m and heading within 20 degrees of 0.

```prediction
# relies on: none
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.1, 1.0]
label = "outside"
[prediction.when]
level = 0.5
dur = 1.0
ch = 0
```

### H2: Channel c3 or c4 drives the body forward

WHEN c3 is held at 1.0 for the first 1.0 s and all other channels are 0, THE system SHALL end with x between 0.1 and 1.0 m.

```prediction
# relies on: E1
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.1, 1.0]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
level = 1.0
dur = 1.0
ch = 3
```

E1 notes: c0 and c2 at 0.5 for 1 s gave x about 0. c1 gave a 4.4 degree turn.

E2 notes: c3 at 1.0 gave x 0.006 and heading 5.2. c4 and c0 gave about 0. Constant pulses do not move the body forward.

### H3: An oscillating channel produces forward travel

WHEN one channel is driven by a 2 Hz sine of amplitude 1.0 for the whole trial and the others are 0, THE system SHALL end with x between 0.1 and 2.0 m for at least one of c0, c2 and c4.

```prediction
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.1, 2.0]
label = "outside"
[prediction.when]
amp = 1.0
freq = 2.0
ch = 0
```
